  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-07-14T23:01:20.125Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Keyboard is able to use gestures with shift+(F1 - F8) But you are unable to on a non-VR controller, e.g. X-box Controller. The D-pad is unused to my knowledge, and could easily be used for gesturing.\n\nMaybe a \"Hold for more options\" button could be implemented for this use; for example a trigger button, \"LT\" isn't used unless you hold an object, or you could press the right stick.\n\nYou have four gestures on your D-pad, and while holding down a button, you could access the other four. Not that I know how this works, but in VR I see people gesturing with both hands, while Desktop can only do one, and you therefore have more options in vr... if I'm not misunderstanding it completely. \n\nBut if I continue writing with that concept in mind, Maybe have a button to toggle which hand you're gesturing with, both for keyboard, and for controller, though only for keyboard works, since Controller has the bonus of being able to rotate objects.\n\nTo wrap this up and explain why I want this; I am using a setup in where I am using a Samsung GearVR with my phone, and an X-box Controller, This gives me control over the head, but I can't use Gestures anymore, they get disabled. so being able to use gestures with the controller would make my VRChat experience way better... atleast make me able to emote more than just tilting my head... which is fun in on in it self, but having gestures would make it better...\n\nI believe I have basicly said the same thing a couple of times now, just phrasing it differently. So I think I am gonna end this post now... \nYours truly ~ ~\nPrincess Toadstool\n                            Peach",
